 "title": "Lower Stakes Mean Higher Competition",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator claims that lower-priced items and entry-level positions face much higher competition than expensive products or senior roles. To escape this competition, you must focus on differentiation, whether you are a startup, employee, or student.",
 "key_points": [
  "A 40 rupees Coca-Cola bottle faces more market competition than a 40,000 watch.",
  "A fresher applying for their first job faces way more competition than a senior manager making 10x more salary.",
  "Lower the stakes, higher the competition.",
  "Lower stakes require you to compete more for differentiation.",
  "To escape competition, you have to start with differentiation.",
  "Be different, escape the competition, and increase the stake."
 ],
 "content": "A 40 rupees Coca-Cola bottle will face more competition in a market than a 40,000 watch will ever will. A fresher applying for his first job in a job market will face way more competition than a senior manager who makes 10X more salary will ever will. Lower the stakes, higher the competition. And the more you have to compete for differentiation. To escape the competition, you have to start with differentiation. Whether you are a startup, an employee or a student. Be different, escape the competition and increase the stake. Hope this helps.",
